WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.230
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.900
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:13.030
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.290
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:22.830
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:28.340
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.220
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.350
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.180
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.140
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.650
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:52.570
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.610
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:00.030
Won't go away

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:03.830
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.960
We believed you

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:14.840
While we stand here

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:19.970
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.780
The Self Defense Force Navy's newest AEGIS class vessel,

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.870
the Mirai, set off from the Yokosuka Base.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.370
Just as we reached deep water,

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.370
the Mirai was struck by a strange weather anomaly...

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.540
...that transported us through time back to June 4th, 1942,

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.380
right in the middle of World War II.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.050
My name is Yosuke Kadomatsu and I am the Mirai's XO,

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.720
the second in command.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.600
I rescued an Imperial Navy intelligence officer named...

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.060
...Takumi Kusaka from certain death.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:19.740
Kusaka is now trying to change the course of history...

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.540
...in order to create a new future different from our own;

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.750
a new world known as Zipang.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.460
What should all 240 SDF crew of the Mirai...

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.590
...be doing in response?

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.380
We have yet to find the answer.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:56.530
The Dead And The Alive

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.440
Welcome back on board, Commander.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.400
- You too, Yanagi.
- Sir.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.940
Captain, how badly were we hit?

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.150
Executive Officer

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.320
5 fatalities.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.400
And 12 more in critical condition.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.240
5... fatalities?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.790
It's all my fault!

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.710
I shouldn't have gone out to that submarine.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.580
I was the one who gave the order for you to go to the Sub.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.630
I'll take full responsibility for it.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.250
And also...

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.880
That Navy Officer.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.100
Even in Japan there will be those...

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.350
...who're opposed to you and the Mirai.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.350
That was what he said to me.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.890
I see.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.440
The Japan that we are headed for...

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.230
...may very well be like a foreign country to us after all.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.900
Even so, every ship needs a port.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:24.360
Commander, whatever awaits us at Yokosuka,

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.160
we will find out when we get there.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.530
Sir! I agree fully.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.580
Good job, both of you.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.580
Go and get some rest.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.380
Sir!

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.810
Darn it!

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.570
Those demons!

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.320
There are 6 launchers in the rear deck,

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.280
is that correct?

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:53.240
6 launchers... No... There might have been more.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.120
There was one main gun,

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.580
and in the rear structure, there's about 10 launchers.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.250
All vertical launch systems, right?

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.750
Yes. And the rockets chased after the planes!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.590
- Hutton.
- Yes...

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.880
It's as if the rockets were alive.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.070
Jones!!

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.370
J-Jones!?

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:04.520
Hutton, get some rest.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.190
We'll do this tomorrow.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.530
In just 2 minutes, 30 planes went down.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.240
And with just one rocket from them,

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.200
the Wasp was!

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.040
Lieutenant,

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.210
the United States Navy...

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.250
Against that monster...

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.670
We don't have a chance.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.260
Hutton.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.720
You must not say that to anyone, no matter what.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.300
The smell of blood has lured...

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.470
...these mosquitoes to the wounded.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.600
Some are too weak to even try to fend them off.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:24.150
We've run out of rice,

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.860
and all we now have for food are weeds,

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:30.530
some rotten coconuts, and if we're lucky, sweet potatoes.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.740
What's more,

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:34.530
we're out of malaria medicine and mosquito nets.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:37.320
Even Tsuji, who was in such high spirits when he arrived,

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.580
is now just a shell of a man.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.670
Tsuji Masanobu, the Commander in the Nomohan Incident,

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.960
known as the God of Strategy after the Malayan Conquest...

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:54.510
Even a man like him...

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:58.050
...is unable to turn the tide here.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.220
Mr. Kadomatsu,

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:04.640
Guadalcanal is turning into a hell just as you predicted.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.440
30 hours,

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:10.650
communications received an incoming message...

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.490
...from a submarine!

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:16.660
The rest of Ichiki's men will not be landing at Guadalcanal.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.280
They're making a retreat!

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.800
The only person who is capable of...

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.550
...preventing the eventual unconditional surrender of Japan,

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.300
is you, Chief Tsuji Masanobu!

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:43.810
So are you asking me to lead our forces on Guadalcanal then?

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.940
Guadalcanal is the decisive battle...

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:49.060
...that will decide the outcome of this war.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.820
Only you may be able to secure a victory.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:00.370
The Japanese Soldiers are the strongest in the world!

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.830
We have nothing to fear!

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.830
We will wipe out all the Americans!!

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.590
Forward!!

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.750
I was tricked by that man!

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.460
He told me this was my big chance!

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.250
He said that if I were able to be victorious here,

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.760
I would become the national hero that...

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.920
...rescued Japan from defeat.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.550
Ridiculous stories about a ship from 60 years into the future?!

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.810
How did I fall for that?!

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:10.100
I fell for his silly stories, and now look where I am!

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.940
L-Look at the pathetic state I'm in now!!

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.610
I also met a man.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:16.610
A crewman from that ship.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.200
According to that man,

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.490
the battle of Guadalcanal will be a huge defeat.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.830
21 thousand soldiers and...

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.210
...4 thousand naval officers...

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:35.250
...will die here, mainly from disease and hunger.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:37.760
Even though we are in dire straits...

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:41.090
...without food or medicine, the Imperial High Command...

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.800
...fails to understand and will not send us supplies.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.430
Without more food and ammo,

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:50.020
the Japanese soldiers will surely be devoured by...

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:54.310
...the mosquitoes and ants on this island.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.940
That was what he told me.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:01.530
Lieutenant Okamura,

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.950
do you believe what that man said?

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:06.660
I only met him briefly,

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:09.950
but I felt he was a good man whom I could trust.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:13.830
No, whoever that man was,

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.960
there's nothing to do but to believe him,

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.090
as everything that he predicted is coming to pass.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.550
Captain Tsuji,

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:26.390
is there anything that we can do to reduce casualties?

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:31.930
Sir!

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.940
Enemy troops discovered...

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.730
...crossing the Matanikau River!

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.860
Company-strength with 3 tanks!

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.530
Good job! They've come...

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:42.900
All troops prepare to retreat!

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.700
We must fall back!

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.120
Carry all the sick and wounded if you have to!

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.080
- Leave no one behind!
- Sir!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.210
Captain?

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.550
Captain Tsuji!

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:04.970
I no longer care whether Japan wins or loses in this war.

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.050
Victory and defeat are...

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.260
...nothing but mere illusions to me now.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.060
Please come with me, Captain Tsuji!

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.310
This isn't like you!

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.310
I think I shall die right here!

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.940
Together with the spirit of our brave troops...

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.520
What're you talking about?!

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:19.690
I don't care if you choose to die here,

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.360
but you're a Japanese officer with responsibilities!

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.900
If you die, you'll cause problems for us!

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.910
Your mission is to make a report on Guadalcanal to the...

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:29.700
...Imperial High Command about our hopeless position!

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:32.040
If it's a report from the "Hero of Malaya",

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.750
everyone's sure to listen!

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.750
Get a hold of yourself, man!

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:38.830
You have to put a stop to this mission and get us out of here!

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.840
Victory or defeat doesn't matter now!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.260
What's important is that we survive!

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:46.380
You're the only one here who can save...

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:48.760
...the lives of our 25 thousand men!!

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.390
I understand now!

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:58.480
The deed of valor that Kusaka mentioned...

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.860
...isn't winning this battle!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:05.070
It's to save the lives of 25 thousand men!

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.200
To convince High Command to evacuate us,

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.830
and avoid a total defeat on this damn island!

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.870
That's equivalent to a victory!

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.750
It's dangerous to stay here, Lieutenant Okamura!

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.380
Let's go!! Hurry up!

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.380
It's about time he got his act together...

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.260
Mr. Kadomatsu,

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:30.970
it looks like we still have a choice in determining our future.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:34.220
Let us all live our lives without any regrets.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.310
We'll retreat now!

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.900
Come on and move!!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.150
If you can't walk, speak up!

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:44.940
No one is to be left behind, you hear!!

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.080
Is Kikuchi in the CIC?

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.290
No, he's in his room.

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.250
- He's asleep.
- He's asleep?

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.460
Yes.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.250
I asked the medics to...

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.210
...give him a sedative.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:09.760
Right now, he's feeling guilt like we did after Guadalcanal.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.550
I'll go check on the injured.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:22.400
What are we going to do now, I wonder?

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:24.690
Oh, according to history,

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:28.360
- the American Pacific fleet will...
- I'm not talking about that.

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:31.320
We've realized the ugly truth.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.620
To survive in this era,

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:36.160
we have to fight and take lives.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:51.010
Out of the 128 men of the 6th squadron,

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:53.390
only 45 remain.

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:01.230
That ship threw out some life preservers before leaving.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:02.770
Perhaps there are...

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.900
Captain!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.900
Oh, Dewitt. What is it?

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.900
It's a miracle.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.450
He was very lucky to have ejected in time,

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.500
and then we found him still floating around in the ocean.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:25.330
There's no mistake!

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.300
It's Jones!!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:31.550
He's still unconscious and suffering from serious burns,

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.550
his pulse is very weak.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.800
The chances of a recovery are...

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:43.310
He's still alive!!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:48.820
Jones?!

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.530
Jones, it's me! It's Hutton! Can you hear me?!

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.950
What is it? What're you trying to say?!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.240
C-Captain.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.790
Reporting in.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.910
Yes. You've done a good job!

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:05.290
- It's a promise.
- What?

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.790
It's a promise.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:11.510
The 2 thousand dollar... cheque.

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:13.470
Ah! Yes!

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:16.760
Don't you worry! I brought it back with me!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.300
We'll go to that great bar in Townsville!

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.600
And we'll really party the whole night there!

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:08.190
I've just lost my best friend.

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:12.570
I wonder if the pain I inflicted on that monster,

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.900
is anywhere near as much as the pain I'm feeling now.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.620
Quite a lot of areas are going to be...

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:26.330
...impossible to repair without a drydock.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.330
You can see the damage we took on the superstructure.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:34.550
From 2000 meters up,

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.340
the Dauntless came in fast and hard...

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:39.640
He was an incredible pilot.

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.350
I see.

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:46.350
And over here. Nashida was standing...

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.230
...right next to me when the plane hit...

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:52.110
He was a good officer,

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.110
and a really nice guy.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:59.700
Hurry up, over here!

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:15.000
Hey? Isn't that Oume?

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:17.010
How rare it is...

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:20.630
...to see CIC personnel come out of their cave for some sun.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:23.640
In times like this, it's not a bad idea to work some stress out?

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:29.310
I'll go for a run after I've checked on...

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.770
...the repairs on Deck 1.

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:32.440
I feel like I've gotten all soft.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.440
Yes.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.730
Corporal Asou.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.570
Yes?

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.990
Did Nashida say anything before he died?

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.950
Ah, no, nothing.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:47.950
I see.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:51.790
I feel that I'm still alive because...

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.750
...of some fortunate coincidence.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:58.420
The reason I'm still standing here talking to you...

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.800
...is because I was in the right place at the right time.

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:08.350
We can't ever predict when we are going to die.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:13.520
In other words, we should make the best of the time we have.

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:17.480
I guess so.

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:19.530
Sir!

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.740
Just as I thought, the death of...

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:29.490
...5 crew members has depressed the entire crew.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.710
Hey! We're running out of nuts!

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:36.920
Got it!

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.840
However, they seem to be doing pretty well...

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:43.470
Is it because they've become numb after facing death head-on?

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.680
We have to get that weld done by today!

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:48.100
We can't dock at Yokosuka looking like this, can we?!

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:54.730
No. Just like Corporal Asou said,

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:56.440
these men have realized they are here...

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:58.320
...because we've been lucky so far.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.560
To control your destiny...

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:37.810
That's a privilege for those who're alive.

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:41.900
They've realized this,

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:45.070
and are getting on with their lives and duties...

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:47.410
As they try to overcome the sadness after...

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:50.410
...the loss of 5 members of our family.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.880
Yes, we're doing just fine...

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:17.530
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.670 --> 00:22:22.770
Just peacefully

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:34.580
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.720 --> 00:22:47.460
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:54.070
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.640 --> 00:23:00.140
I kept on praying

00:23:01.540 --> 00:23:11.990
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:27.670
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:42.140
We've come home at last.

00:23:42.140 --> 00:23:43.220
I'm surprised.

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:46.470
To think Mitsumasa Yonai come aboard by himself!

00:23:46.470 --> 00:23:48.230
But I am someone who can't turn a blind eye...

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:51.060
...to the loss of even one person's life if it can be prevented!

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:53.940
I can't just let those people die for no reason!

00:23:53.940 --> 00:23:56.480
Lieutenant Tsuda, I must tell you something...

00:23:56.480 --> 00:23:58.570
...before I leave Japan.

00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:00.280
I think...

00:24:00.280 --> 00:24:02.700
...the best way forward would be for this ship...

00:24:00.320 --> 00:24:05.240
Next Episode: The Return

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:05.040
...to be blown up and scuttled in Yoksuka harbor!

00:24:05.240 --> 00:24:10.170
This story is purely fiction. The names of the characters and organizations that appear have no connections with actual people and organizations.
